{"id": "unknown-2026-11-18-006", "date": "2026-11-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.75, "keywords": ["decline", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Polyester & viscose yarn prices decline in India amid sluggish demand", "content": "Polyester and viscose yarn prices fell across major Indian markets as weak demand, payment constraints and lower raw material costs hit sentiment.\nLudhiana and Surat saw polyester yarn weaken, while viscose yarn eased in Mumbai and Surat on subdued buying and higher imports.\nNorth Indian cotton prices also eased as post-Diwali arrivals rose and falling ICE futures weighed on exporters.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/polyester-viscose-yarn-prices-decline-in-india-amid-sluggish-demand-315133-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-18-007", "date": "2026-11-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India ITME 2026 to showcase textile technology in Greater Noida", "content": "India ITME 2026 will bring textile machinery and technology providers to Greater Noida from 4–9 December for its 12th edition.\nCovering spinning to garment manufacturing, the exhibition will spotlight automation, sustainability and modernisation.\nTextile Horizons on 5–6 December will feature a CEO conclave, technical awards and networking, with over 250 decision-makers and delegates expected.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-itme-2026-to-showcase-textile-technology-in-greater-noida-315132-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-18-008", "date": "2026-11-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton futures recover marginally on bargain buying, firm grains", "content": "ICE cotton futures recovered modestly, with March 2027 up 48 points at 81.40 cents per pound, but gains stayed limited by a firm US dollar.\nBargain buying, stronger grains and higher crude oil supported prices after Monday’s sharp fall near recent lows.\nVolume fell to 70,485 contracts, certified stocks rose to 84,978 bales, and traders watched December liquidation before November 23.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-futures-recover-marginally-on-bargain-buying-firm-grains-315109-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-18-009", "date": "2026-11-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India’s apparel exports to US fall 20.5%: Can it win back buyers?", "content": "India’s readymade garment exports rose 20.33 per cent year on year to $1.287 billion in October 2026, but April-October exports remained 2.97 per cent lower and US-bound shipments fell sharply.\nThe rebound follows a weak October 2025 base, with the latest value only 4.8 per cent above October 2024.\nNo India-specific US tariff advantage is confirmed without an implemented apparel schedule.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/india-s-apparel-exports-to-us-fall-20-5-can-it-win-back-buyers--315125-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-18-010", "date": "2026-11-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth", "increase", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "US' Amer Sports raises 2026 outlook as Q3 revenue climbs 24%", "content": "Amer Sports raised its FY26 revenue growth outlook to 25-26 per cent after third-quarter revenue increased 24 per cent to $2.17 billion. \nNet income attributable to equity holders rose 67 per cent to $240 million, while adjusted operating margin improved to 16.4 per cent. \nTechnical Apparel and Outdoor Performance posted revenue growth of 26 per cent and 27 per cent, respectively. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/us-amer-sports-raises-2026-outlook-as-q3-revenue-climbs-24--315108-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-18-011", "date": "2026-11-18", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 47, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["delay"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Could Bangladesh’s ongoing labour protest impact sourcing dynamics?", "content": "Bangladesh garment protests have shut around 65 factories in Savar, Ashulia and Gazipur as workers seek a minimum wage rise to Taka 32,000 (~$256).\nAnother 56 reportedly declared holidays, deepening disruption after an energy crisis in a sector employing over four million and earning 80 per cent of merchandise exports.\nSustained delays could divert orders to India and hit Indian yarn suppliers.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/could-bangladesh-s-ongoing-labour-protest-impact-sourcing-dynamics--315037-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
